# Presence of this file lets `qs ipc call lock submit <passphrase>` reach the
# lock surface's ordinary PAM conversation, so the in-VM gate can prove that a
# CORRECT passphrase actually unlocks a session — the one property the lock
# screen exists for, and the one nothing had ever tested.
#
# It is not an unlock bypass: a wrong secret fails exactly as it does at the
# keyboard and faillock counts it the same way. It is a guessing surface, which
# is why it ships here and only here.
#
# This file must never appear in a release tree. check-release-image.sh
# assertion A15 fails the build if it does.
